        "kind": "window",
        "band": null,
        "text": "The algebra predicts that each failed request starts in a window. The window opens at the fault, and it closes 9.98 s to 10 s after the fault. Each failed request ends with a timeout. With n sessions on the target at the fault, the window closes n × 10 ms to n × 45 ms later. The failed requests are those of the n sessions up to the end of the window without this term, at the measured mean period of the clients, and 0 to 3 more for each session. Each session also fails a request each turn until the window closes: 0 to n × the largest drain time over its turn, rounded up. One session can drain for up to 100 ms, thus the window closes up to (n − 1) × 45 ms + 100 ms later. The last failed request can start up to one turn before the window closes."
      },
